# SSAS Environment Configuration
# =========================================================
# This file documents the required configuration values.
#
# Since SSAS is a pure static HTML project (no Node.js build),
# these values cannot be loaded from a .env file at runtime.
#
# ACTION REQUIRED:
#   Open js/supabase-client.js and replace the placeholder
#   values with your actual Supabase project credentials.
#
# HOW TO GET THESE VALUES:
#   1. Go to https://supabase.com and log in
#   2. Open your project
#   3. Navigate to Settings → API
#   4. Copy "Project URL" and "anon public" key
#
# See SUPABASE_SETUP.md for full instructions.
# =========================================================

# Your Supabase project URL
# Example: https://abcxyz123.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=YOUR_SUPABASE_PROJECT_URL

# Your Supabase anon (public) key — SAFE to expose in browser
# Example: eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY

# =========================================================
# ❌ DO NOT use or expose the service_role key:
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<never put this in frontend code>
# =========================================================
